  "ownershipAndDataflow": [
    "Constructor alone reads output/root/source-selection/planning-context and approved transitive reference schema files. A construction-local static input map ensures each required ref tree belongs to this same instance epoch; it contains no supplied request/context/source/credentials.",
    "Constructor builds every current Kind with original alternatives/reference/provider keyword projection and unchanged count/compact/Shape algorithms; then final private Map.copyOf static inputs/providers and final private provenance complete before constructor returns. Intermediate locals and this are never registered/published; failure prevents publication.",
    "Map.copyOf prevents structural map mutation. JsonNodes remain privately owned: constructor-only builders never run from public getters, providers/provenance return new deepCopy on EVERY call. No private mutable node escapes; output is immutable original String.",
    "The configured SourceClassifier receives SAME existing GuidedPromptAssembler bean as TranslationService. Compatible three-argument classifier constructor creates one assembler during its own construction and delegates; classify reads that instance, never constructs per call. Current policy/source/classification body changes only schemaPins provider expression.",
    "Existing TranslationService/request getters, pin comparisons, source/permission/owner/fence/budget/clock/SQL/CAS/accounting/provider paths and planning spy assertions remain outside candidate scope and unchanged."
  ],
  "acceptedErrorAndLifetimeSemantics": [
    "Static missing/malformed/transitive/reference/canonical failures now fail assembler construction/startup, including unconditional bean and old classifier constructor fallback. No partial/fallback bundle; this is explicitly accepted lifetime change, not second-resource-read equivalence.",
    "Static resources changing after construction require new instance/application context restart. No deployed FS/image immutability or DevTools exact watcher behavior claimed. Per-request source/auth/owner/catalog/policy freshness remains original; no dynamic authority cache.",
    "Current output/schema/$defs/Shape/canonical/hash identities are source-proven preserved for identical packaged bytes; runtime baseline parity remains UNRUN. No shape/string/hash fixture/generator/pin/migration edits or performance/PASS promise."
  ],
